From caddd3daa54945674020dbb9c98a62178dbf6e39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 0racl-lab <360770237+0racl-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:30:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] read_evm_log: return blockNumber and blockTimestamp

Matches the qubic/core EvmLogRead change that appends two fields to the
reply (440 -> 456 bytes):

  blockNumber     uint64 [440..448)  block that includes the transaction
  blockTimestamp  uint64 [448..456)  that block's timestamp (Unix seconds)

The timestamp is read from the block the receipt names, fetched by hash
on every endpoint; the block's hash and number must match the receipt and
every endpoint must report the same timestamp, otherwise the service
abstains. Existing fields and result codes are unchanged.

Selftest: checks the new fields, abstains when providers disagree only on
the timestamp (new --tamper-time mock flag) or cannot return the block.
Deploy together with the core release that carries the new reply size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QHXGjDwxBARUytE2smA8oq
